              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='16410' id='16' type-v2='text' w='99064' x='468' y='82697'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontsize='14' underline='true'>Key Findings</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>- North America is the largest market almost every year, at about half of global sales.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>- Japan had a large share in the 1980-90s, which shrank steadily afterwards.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>- Europe&apos;s share grew overtime and came close to North America&apos;s in the 2010s.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontsize='12'>- Total sales peaked at around 2008-2009. The drop after that is partly because the dataset stops collecting data.</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
